Analyze this {language} code for SLAP (Single Level of Abstraction Principle) violations.

Source file:
{source}

Return a JSON array of violations:
{{
  "function": "function name",
  "line": <line number>,
  "severity": "high|medium|low",
  "violation": "mixed abstraction levels: high-level X alongside low-level Y",
  "suggestion": "extract low-level details into helper function"
}}

SLAP: each function should operate at one level of abstraction.
Violation: a function that calls high-level orchestration methods (ProcessOrder, SendEmail)
  alongside low-level implementation details (parsing strings, bit manipulation, SQL queries).

Return [] if no violations. Return ONLY the JSON array.
